question:
In a factor tree, each node is the product of the two values below it unless a value is already at its prime form. Compute the value of $A$ in the factor tree shown:

[asy]
draw((-1,-.3)--(0,0)--(1,-.3),linewidth(1));
draw((-2,-1.3)--(-1.5,-.8)--(-1,-1.3),linewidth(1));
draw((1,-1.3)--(1.5,-.8)--(2,-1.3),linewidth(1));
label("A",(0,0),N);
label("B",(-1.5,-.8),N);
label("4",(-2,-1.3),S);
label("C",(1.5,-.8),N);
label("D",(-1,-1.3),S);
label("7",(1,-1.3),S);
label("E",(2,-1.3),S);
draw((-1.5,-2.3)--(-1,-1.8)--(-.5,-2.3),linewidth(1));
draw((1.5,-2.3)--(2,-1.8)--(2.5,-2.3),linewidth(1));
label("4",(-1.5,-2.3),S);
label("3",(-.5,-2.3),S);
label("7",(1.5,-2.3),S);
label("3",(2.5,-2.3),S);
[/asy]

Given the function $f(x)=\sqrt{3}{\cos^{2}}x-\sin x\cos (\pi -x)$, $x\in R$.

(1) Find the smallest positive period and monotonic interval of $f(x)$;

(2) Find the maximum and minimum values of $f(x)$ in the interval $\left[-\dfrac{\pi }{4}, \dfrac{\pi }{4}\right]$.

## Subject III. (20 points)

Let $E_{1}=\frac{a(2 a+8)+8}{(a+4)(2 a+12)-16}$ and $E_{2}=\frac{a(a+4)+4}{a(a+1)-2}$.

a) Determine $a \in \mathbb{Z}$ such that the expressions make sense;

b) Determine $a \in \mathbb{Z}$ for which $\frac{1}{E_{1}}+\frac{1}{E_{2}} \in \mathbb{N}$;

c) Calculate $a \in \mathbb{Z}$ such that $\frac{1}{E_{1}}+\frac{1}{E_{2}}=\frac{3 a+10}{a+2}$.

Prof. Simona Pop, Colegiul Augustin Maior Cluj-Napoca

The graph of $y=g(x)$ is shown, with $1$ unit between grid lines. Assume $g(x)$ is defined only on the domain shown. Determine the sum of all integers $c$ for which the equation $g(x)=c$ has exactly $4$ solutions.

[asy]
size(150);
real ticklen=3;
real tickspace=2;

real ticklength=0.1cm;
real axisarrowsize=0.14cm;
pen axispen=black+1.3bp;
real vectorarrowsize=0.2cm;
real tickdown=-0.5;
real tickdownlength=-0.15inch;
real tickdownbase=0.3;
real wholetickdown=tickdown;
void rr_cartesian_axes(real xleft, real xright, real ybottom, real ytop, real xstep=1, real ystep=1, bool useticks=false, bool complexplane=false, bool usegrid=true) {

import graph;

real i;

if(complexplane) {

label("$\textnormal{Re}$",(xright,0),SE);

label("$\textnormal{Im}$",(0,ytop),NW);

} else {

label("$x$",(xright+0.4,-0.5));

label("$y$",(-0.5,ytop+0.2));

}

ylimits(ybottom,ytop);

xlimits( xleft, xright);

real[] TicksArrx,TicksArry;

for(i=xleft+xstep; i0.1) {

TicksArrx.push(i);

}

}

for(i=ybottom+ystep; i0.1) {

TicksArry.push(i);

}

}

if(usegrid) {

xaxis(BottomTop(extend=false), Ticks("%", TicksArrx ,pTick=gray(0.22),extend=true),p=invisible);

yaxis(LeftRight(extend=false),Ticks("%", TicksArry ,pTick=gray(0.22),extend=true), p=invisible);

}

if(useticks) {

xequals(0, ymin=ybottom, ymax=ytop, p=axispen, Ticks("%",TicksArry , pTick=black+0.8bp,Size=ticklength), above=true, Arrows(size=axisarrowsize));

yequals(0, xmin=xleft, xmax=xright, p=axispen, Ticks("%",TicksArrx , pTick=black+0.8bp,Size=ticklength), above=true, Arrows(size=axisarrowsize));

} else {

xequals(0, ymin=ybottom, ymax=ytop, p=axispen, above=true, Arrows(size=axisarrowsize));

yequals(0, xmin=xleft, xmax=xright, p=axispen, above=true, Arrows(size=axisarrowsize));

}
};
rr_cartesian_axes(-6,6,-7,7);
real g(real x) {return (x-4)*(x-2)*(x+2)*(x+4)/120-2;}
draw(graph(g,-4.5,4.5,operator ..), blue);
[/asy]

Given that the sequence $\{a\_n\}$ is an arithmetic sequence, where $a\_2+a\_3=8$, $a\_5=3a\_2$.
(1) Find the general term formula of the sequence $\{a\_n\}$;
(2) Let $b\_n=\frac{2}{a\_n a_{n+1}}$, and denote the sum of the first $n$ terms of $\{b\_n\}$ as $S\_n$. Find the smallest positive integer $n$ such that $S\_n > \frac{2016}{2017}$.

A region $R$ in the complex plane is defined by \begin{align*}
R = \{x + iy: -2 \le x \le 2, -2 \le y \le 2\}.
\end{align*}
A complex number $z = x + iy$ is chosen uniformly at random from $R$. What is the probability that $\left(\frac{2}{3} + \frac{2}{3}i\right)z$ is also in $R$?

Example 4 (2005 Guangdong College Entrance Examination Question) Given a function $f(x)$ defined on $\mathbf{R}$ that satisfies: for any real number $x$, $f(2+x)=f(2-x)$, $f(7+x)=f(7-x)$, and in the interval $[0,7]$, only $f(1)=f(3)=0$.
(1) Determine the odd or even nature of $f(x)$;
(2) Find the number of roots of the equation $f(x)=0$ in the interval $[-2005,2005]$.

Let $f(x) = 
\begin{cases} 
2e^{x-1}, & \text{if } x < 2,\\
\log_{3}(2^{x}-1), & \text{if } x \geq 2
\end{cases}
$, then $f(f(2))$ equals \_\_\_\_\_.

A 3x3 magic square grid has the numbers and variables as shown, with $w$, $y$, $a$, $b$, and $z$ as variables. Find $a+b$. 

[asy]
path a=(0,0)--(1,0)--(1,1)--(0,1)--cycle;
for (int i=0; i<3; ++i) {
for (int j=0; j<3; ++j) {
draw(shift((i,j))*a);
};}
label("19",(0.5,0.3),N);
label("$w$",(1.5,0.3),N);
label("23",(2.5,0.3),N);
label("22",(0.5,1.3),N);
label("$y$",(1.5,1.3),N);
label("$a$",(2.5,1.3),N);
label("$b$",(0.5,2.3),N);
label("18",(1.5,2.3),N);
label("$z$",(2.5,2.3),N);
[/asy]

Each of the boxes in the figure below is a square. The figure is formed by a 6x6 grid of lines. How many different squares can be traced using the lines in the figure?

[asy]
unitsize(0.2inch);
draw((0,0)--(6,0)--(6,6)--(0,6)--cycle);
for (int i=1; i<6; ++i) {
    draw((i,0)--(i,6));
    draw((0,i)--(6,i));
}
[/asy]

Given that the sum of the coefficients of all terms in the expansion of the binomial $\left(x+\frac{1}{x}\right)^n$ is $256$.

(I) Find the value of $n$;

(II) Find the constant term in the expansion. (Answer with a numerical value)
